{"raw": {"https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/34013": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership, Dept. of Secondary Education and Educational Leadership", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership, Dept. of Secondary Education and Educational Leadership Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership, Dept. of Secondary Education and Educational Leadership Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement - Applicants are required to submit a teaching statement that reflects their philosophy and practices related to teaching and learning in higher education. The statement should discuss instructional methods, student engagement, assessment of learning outcomes, and commitment to creating an inclusive, supportive, and effective learning environment for diverse student populations. Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership, Dept. of Secondary Education and Educational Leadership Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Department Summary The Secondary Education and Educational Leadership Department ( SEEL ) at Bridgewater State University is part of a cohesive and diverse campus community that provides professional opportunities for faculty advancement in teaching and scholarship and a clear path to tenure. Funding for faculty scholarship is available through the Center for the Advancement of Research and Scholarship as well as the Office of Teaching and Learning. There is also a significant institutional commitment to undergraduate research and international engagement. SEEL is committed to supporting diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging among its faculty, staff and students, and to strengthening a justice-informed identity as identified in our strategic plan. This emphasis is reflected throughout the University\u2019s curricular and co-curricular activities. SEEL , as part of Bridgewater State University, is a teaching institution and faculty are committed to their critical role in the successful graduation of our students. The University values scholarship and other ways in which faculty express their professional contributions and accomplishments. This flexibility sustains the need for faculty excellence, while also recognizing the diversity of talents and interests of our faculty as they move up the tenure ladder. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving human condition. Our commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion is reflected in our institutional values , which ensures that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of Secondary Education and Educational Leadership ( SEEL ) invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position. The mission of the department is to prepare educators and related professionals to teach, lead, and serve in a diverse and evolving global society. Successful candidates will be staff members who can collaborate with colleagues to help meet the mission of the department in serving and supporting our ethnically diverse campus community. The successful candidate will educate students primarily in the Educational Leadership ( EDLE ) program, including the Education Specialist, M.Ed., Higher Education Administration, and administrator-licensure programs. Responsibilities may also include student teaching/practicum supervision, teaching advising in other undergraduate and graduate courses in the department. The successful applicant will collaborate with faculty members in the program and the department as well as engage with College of Education and Health Professions colleagues and other internal and external partners in the program assessment, continuous improvement, marketing, and expansion of existing programs through the creation of off-campus cohorts. This position requires contractual scheduled office hours for student advising and consultation. Additional responsibilities may include mentoring graduate students and other related duties as assigned and/or required. The successful candidate will display effective practices for diverse graduate and undergraduate students. Required Qualifications Ph.D. or Ed.D. in Educational Leadership/School Administration \u2014Candidates who have not yet earned their doctoral degree may be considered, but evidence of an impending successful degree conferral by September 1, 2027 will be required. Demonstrated expertise that will contribute to the department\u2019s understanding of P-16 educational leadership, including (but not limited to): school, district, higher education administration, or community leadership; school improvement; and/or organizational development. Ability to teach courses on educational leadership, organizational change, education finance, or education law for students who are both K-12 and higher education professionals in synchronous, asynchronous, hybrid, and face-to-face modalities. Five or more years of experience in PK-12/16 school administration. Demonstrated ability to design and teach online graduate and undergraduate courses utilizing effective online/hybrid teaching strategies to promote student learning. A record of excellence in teaching, service, and or scholarship that demonstrates a commitment to a multicultural work environment that celebrates multiple perspectives. Preferred Qualifications Experience and commitment to advising, recruiting, and/or mentoring graduate students. Evidence of qualitative, quantitative, or mixed-methods research. Experience in program assessment, state, and national accreditation standards. Commitment to excellence in teaching and advising, and to professional work in a multicultural environment that embraces excellence, diversity, and multiple perspectives. Experience with State, National, and Professional accreditation Standards. MA standards preferred. Record of professional activities commensurate with the rank of assistant professor. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. At present, the university can only sponsor employment-based visas, including H1-B petitions, that are not subject to the current $100,000 fee or any other similar or related fees imposed through U.S. immigration regulations, laws, executive orders, etc. The university will continue to monitor the ongoing changes in U.S. immigration regulations and it reserves the right to modify this policy as the regulatory and legal landscapes change. Salary is commensurate with experience in accordance with the Appendix O of the MSCA contract . A reasonable starting salary range to expect for a new faculty member appointed at the rank of Assistant Professor is $75,000 to $85,000. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00658P Open Date 09/28/2026 Close Date 11/02/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement - Applicants are required to submit a teaching statement that reflects their philosophy and practices related to teaching and learning in higher education. The statement should discuss instructional methods, student engagement, assessment of learning outcomes, and commitment to creating an inclusive, supportive, and effective learning environment for diverse student populations. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/34004": {"title": "Assistant Professors of Cyber Security and Computer Science , Department of Computer Science", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Assistant Professors of Cyber Security and Computer Science , Department of Computer Science Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Assistant Professors of Cyber Security and Computer Science , Department of Computer Science Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement- In the teaching statement, please describe your teaching experience and interest in using engaged and inclusive pedagogical approaches and working with diverse student populations. An instructional artifact, such as a syllabus, lesson plan or other materials that demonstrate a capacity to engage with and support students with varied backgrounds and learning styles Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professors of Cyber Security and Computer Science , Department of Computer Science Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Department Summary The Department of Computer Science at Bridgewater State University invites applications for one tenure-track position in computer science with primary consideration for software engineering, operating systems and computer architecture, cloud computing or theory of computation; and one tenure-track position in cybersecurity with primary consideration for software security, operating system security, or hardware security, beginning September 2027. The successful candidates will join our dynamic and collaborative department to contribute to teaching, advising, scholarly and service activities. We are a mid-sized, cordial, collaborative, and innovative group of thirteen full-time faculty members, with a strong tradition of supporting, mentoring, and helping one another. Our department prepares students for exciting careers and graduate school through high quality instruction in small classes and close collaboration between faculty members and students on projects. Our goal is to provide students with a strong foundation in the fields of computer science and cybersecurity, one that also promotes critical thinking and lifetime learning. In Fall 2025, 45% of our declared majors were students of color, 48% were first-generation, 34% were low-income, and 10% were LGBTQIA+. Our department offers a Bachelor of Science in computer science, which is ABET accredited. A new Bachelor of Science in cybersecurity and digital forensics was launched in Fall 2024 to meet a high regional demand. Our department also offers minors in computer science, computer engineering, and cybersecurity & digital forensics. In addition, we also offer a Master of Science in computer science. The department is housed in the Dana Mohler-Faria Science and Mathematics Center, where faculty and staff work with students in electronics, robotics, and computer labs, with a new cyber range established to extend student learning. Bridgewater State University has hosted programming competitions and is starting to serve as a regional center for cybersecurity in Massachusetts. Successful candidates will work with colleagues to support the needs of all students in our inclusive community. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties Essential Duties Responsibilities include teaching both introductory and advanced courses in computer science and/or cybersecurity, advising undergraduates and supervising MS students, participating in university and departmental service including curriculum development and ABET accreditation work, as well as engaging in ongoing scholarship and professional activity. The candidate must demonstrate sensitivity to and understanding of students from diverse backgrounds with a wide range of abilities. Required Qualifications Required Qualifications Applicants should have an earned Ph.D. in computer science or cybersecurity or a closely related STEM field such as computer engineering, information technology, applied math, or electrical engineering with a focus in computer science or cybersecurity by September 1, 2027. Alternatively, applicants with an earned Ph.D. in other relevant STEM fields are welcomed provided they have significant industry experience in computer science or cybersecurity and a solid technical background. ABD applicants will be considered so long as the candidate has the Ph.D. in hand by September 1, 2027. Candidates should also demonstrate excellent verbal and written communications skills. Use of AI tools for grammar and editing is acceptable . However, it is important for the search committee to hear each candidate\u2019s own voice to understand and know the candidate. Application materials should reflect your own ideas, experiences, and writing, which are considered as the evidence of good communication skills. Finalists will be asked to discuss their materials in depth. A demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching, advising and student research mentoring that enhances an equitable and inclusive learning and working environment. Candidates should demonstrate established capacity for scholarly contribution. Preferred Qualifications Preferred Qualifications While extremely strong candidates of all specialties will be considered, primary consideration will be given to those with specialties in software engineering, operating systems and computer architecture, cloud computing or theory of computation for one tenure-track position in computer science; and software security, operating system security, or hardware security for one tenure-track position in cybersecurity. Candidates who involve undergraduates in research and projects are especially encouraged to apply. Additional preferred qualifications include: Previous college teaching experiences in post-secondary institutions in related fields. Commitment to student development through teaching, advising, and mentoring that align with BSU\u2019s dedication to equity and values. Knowledge of or openness to developing culturally responsive and effective practices to engage a diverse group of students. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. At present, the university can only sponsor employment-based visas, including H1-B petitions, that are not subject to the current $100,000 fee or any other similar or related fees imposed through U.S. immigration regulations, laws, executive orders, etc. The university will continue to monitor the ongoing changes in U.S. immigration regulations and it reserves the right to modify this policy as the regulatory and legal landscapes change. Salary is commensurate with experience in accordance with the Appendix O of the MSCA contract . A reasonable starting salary range to expect for a new faculty member appointed at the rank of Assistant Professor is $75,000 to $85,000. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00662P Open Date 10/08/2026 Close Date 11/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement- In the teaching statement, please describe your teaching experience and interest in using engaged and inclusive pedagogical approaches and working with diverse student populations. An instructional artifact, such as a syllabus, lesson plan or other materials that demonstrate a capacity to engage with and support students with varied backgrounds and learning styles Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Other Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33989": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Management with a concentration in Management Information Systems, Department of Management and Marketing", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Assistant Professor of Management with a concentration in Management Information Systems, Department of Management and Marketing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Assistant Professor of Management with a concentration in Management Information Systems, Department of Management and Marketing Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement including experience with diverse populations. Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor of Management with a concentration in Management Information Systems, Department of Management and Marketing Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Department Summary The Management & Marketing Department is seeking a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Management with a concentration in Management Information Systems. We offer courses and experiential learning to students who want careers involving information systems, business analytics, technology management, and data-informed decision-making in private, public, and not-for-profit organizations. Through flexible programs, students complete coursework in either in-person classes, real-time online courses at a scheduled time, or autonomously. Our department is supportive and engaging, offering a place for a successful candidate to thrive. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the Commonwealth, and the world. BSU has worked to ensure that our students receive an accessible, affordable, and exceptional education. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Those committed to working in a diverse cultural environment are strongly encouraged to apply. Essential Duties The Department of Management and Marketing invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position teaching an array of Management Information Systems courses, including fundamentals of information systems, business analytics, data visualization, database management, AI and other current topics related to information systems and emerging technologies. Ideal candidates are willing to grow with our evolving program and have a commitment to excellence in teaching, advising, and student engagement. The successful candidate may occasionally teach a variety of Management courses. Responsibilities of the position include teaching upper-level and lower-level courses, with the opportunity to teach Honors and graduate courses, both online and traditional face-to-face, for our University\u2019s diverse student population using a variety of appropriate and engaging teaching methods. Department faculty members are expected to participate in advising students on academic curricula; maintain regularly scheduled office hours for student consultation and engagement; serve on faculty committees; participate in faculty meetings; participate in the development of departmental curricula; and adhere to all institutional policies. Required Qualifications Ph.D. or DBA in Management Information Systems, Information Systems, Business Analytics, or a directly related field from a regionally accredited university by September 1, 2027, is required. Experience effectively presenting information systems, business analytics, or technology-related concepts, for example through teaching courses, mentoring, professional presentations, or training. Related professional work experience. Preferred Qualifications Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. At present, the university can only sponsor employment-based visas, including H1-B petitions, that are not subject to the current $100,000 fee or any other similar or related fees imposed through U.S. immigration regulations, laws, executive orders, etc. The university will continue to monitor the ongoing changes in U.S. immigration regulations and it reserves the right to modify this policy as the regulatory and legal landscapes change. Salary is commensurate with experience in accordance with the Appendix O of the MSCA contract . A reasonable starting salary range to expect for a new faculty member appointed at the rank of Assistant Professor is $75,000 to $85,000. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00654P Open Date 09/02/2026 Close Date 11/25/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement including experience with diverse populations. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33986": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Department of Political Science - International Relations", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Assistant Professor, Department of Political Science - International Relations Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Assistant Professor, Department of Political Science - International Relations Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter One-page statement of teaching philosophy Sample of scholarly research Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor, Department of Political Science - International Relations Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Department Summary The Department of Political Science at Bridgewater State University ( BSU ) consists of nine full-time faculty members and provides rigorous undergraduate and graduate education. Building on the University\u2019s strong liberal arts foundation, we prepare a diverse student body for leadership roles in public and nonprofit sectors, and the profession of governance. The department\u2019s undergraduate learning outcomes align with the goals of the University\u2019s Strategic Plan ( https://www.bridgew.edu/the-university/strategic-plan-2/strategic-priorities ) and provide for a teaching and learning environment characterized by intellectual, creative, and professional growth. Our learning outcomes include: Critical Analysis of Political Processes, Institutions, & Practices : Students will critically assess the systematic factors that underlie political processes, systems, and practices. Effective Written Communication : Students will effectively communicate about political systems, processes, and theories in a rigorous manner by developing cogent, logical arguments that properly employ and make use of relevant evidence. Diversity, Equity, Inclusion, & Accessibility: Students will be able to: 1) Analyze how dimensions of human diversity (e.g., race, sex, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, class, national origin, citizenship, etc.) shape political attitudes, participation, and outcome, 2) Evaluate the empirical and normative implications of government actions that affect these dynamics, and 3) Assess the conceptual and definitional challenges involved in studying human diversity. Understanding Research Design : Students should understand, apply, and recognize the main processes of research design. Application of Qualitative & Quantitative Research Methods : Students should understand, recognize and know how to apply the primary characteristics of both qualitative and quantitative research. BSU is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the Commonwealth, and the world. BSU\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper meaning. The teaching and learning environments at BSU also cultivate meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and foster appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values, which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Political Science Department at BSU invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in international relations to begin the fall semester 2027 at the level of assistant professor. The successful applicant will be required to teach courses in international relations, American foreign policy, and other courses in the department\u2019s International Affairs concentration. Additionally, the successful applicant will contribute to the department\u2019s responsibilities in the University\u2019s CORE curriculum (including Introduction to American Government as well as First and Second Year Seminars) and the department\u2019s undergraduate research methods sequence. Required Qualifications A Ph.D. in Political Science or a related field by September 1, 2027 is required. A commitment to teaching excellence, and evidence of scholarly activity in the field of international relations are also required. Preferred Qualifications Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. At present, the university can only sponsor employment-based visas, including H1-B petitions, that are not subject to the current $100,000 fee or any other similar or related fees imposed through U.S. immigration regulations, laws, executive orders, etc. The university will continue to monitor the ongoing changes in U.S. immigration regulations and it reserves the right to modify this policy as the regulatory and legal landscapes change. Salary is commensurate with experience in accordance with the Appendix O of the MSCA contract . A reasonable starting salary range to expect for a new faculty member appointed at the rank of Assistant Professor is $75,000 to $85,000. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00647P Open Date 08/01/2026 Close Date 10/16/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter One-page statement of teaching philosophy Sample of scholarly research Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Teaching Statement Other Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33984": {"title": "Assistant Professor, School of Social Work", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Assistant Professor, School of Social Work Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Assistant Professor, School of Social Work Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement For best consideration, please apply by October 4, 2026. Review of applications will begin after this date and continue until the position closes on November 1, 2026. Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor, School of Social Work Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Department Summary The School of Social Work at Bridgewater State University ( BSU ) has experienced dynamic growth and invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track teaching position at the rank of Assistant Professor, beginning September 2027. The School of Social Work houses a BSW program and an MSW program. Our BSW and MSW programs are accredited by the Council on Social Work Education ( CSWE ) and enrollment totals approximately 550 students. According to US News & World Report, the School of Social Work is ranked in the top 100 Schools of Social Work at number 83. The School of Social Work ( SSW ) at Bridgewater State University is part of a cohesive campus community that provides professional opportunities for faculty advancement in teaching and scholarship and a clear path to tenure. Funding for faculty scholarship is available through the Center for the Advancement of Research and Scholarship as well as the Office of Teaching and Learning. There is also a significant institutional commitment to undergraduate research and international engagement. The SSW is committed to supporting diversity, equity and inclusion among its faculty, staff and students, and to strengthening a justice-informed identity as identified in our strategic plan. This emphasis is reflected throughout the University\u2019s curricular and co-curricular activities. The School of Social Work is a teaching institution and faculty and field staff members are committed to their critical role in successfully graduating our students. The University values scholarship and other ways in which faculty express their professional contributions and accomplishments. This flexibility sustains the need for faculty excellence, while also recognizing the diversity of talents and interests of our faculty as they move up the tenure ladder. We welcome faculty teaching in field education seminars, especially for those with current or recent past practice experience. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties Teaching responsibilities will be in the undergraduate and/or graduate social work programs. Primary course responsibilities may include: research methods, human behavior and the social environment; the dynamics of diversity and oppression; practice with individuals, families or groups; practice with community; and practicum seminar. Teaching assignments will depend on the expertise of the candidate and programmatic needs. A commitment to working with non-traditional students will require evening and some weekend teaching. Additional responsibilities include student advising, curriculum/program development and assessment, and collaboration on school, college, and university-wide committees. In addition, faculty are encouraged to contribute to leadership within the school as opportunities become available. We are considering the future directions of the School of Social Work and hope to recruit faculty with experience in varied delivery models (online, Hybrid, Hyflex) to complement our on-campus teaching. We also welcome faculty innovation in teaching that includes use of simulation and other pilots/inclusion of ways to assist our student learning. Applicants should be able to demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and advising and to working with a diverse student body. Candidates whose teaching, research, and advising is informed by equity minded practices and a social justice lens are strongly encouraged to apply. Applicants should have the ability to work collaboratively and use technology effectively in teaching and learning. Applicants must demonstrate evidence of scholarly activity and a commitment o public higher education. For best consideration, please apply by October 4, 2026. Review of applications will begin after this date and continue until the position closes on November 1, 2026. Required Qualifications Earned doctorate in Social Work or a closely related field completed and awarded by September 1, 2027. A commitment to equity, inclusion, accessibility, social justice and community engagement, as demonstrated by current research, practice or teaching. Master of social work degree from a CSWE accredited program and at least two years of post- MSW practice experience. Preferred Qualifications Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. At present, the university can only sponsor employment-based visas, including H1-B petitions, that are not subject to the current $100,000 fee or any other similar or related fees imposed through U.S. immigration regulations, laws, executive orders, etc. The university will continue to monitor the ongoing changes in U.S. immigration regulations and it reserves the right to modify this policy as the regulatory and legal landscapes change. Salary is commensurate with experience in accordance with the Appendix O of the MSCA contract . A reasonable starting salary range to expect for a new faculty member appointed at the rank of Assistant Professor is $75,000 to $85,000. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00650P Open Date 08/14/2026 Close Date 11/01/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement For best consideration, please apply by October 4, 2026. Review of applications will begin after this date and continue until the position closes on November 1, 2026. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33981": {"title": "Part-Time Faculty, Department of Geography", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Part-Time Faculty, Department of Geography Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Part-Time Faculty, Department of Geography Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Geography Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Posting Details Position Information Title Part-Time Faculty, Department of Geography Rank Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Department Summary The Department of Geography offers four major concentrations and coordinates three minor programs. Geography majors may choose from a BS major concentration in Environmental Sustainability and Climate Resilience or in Environmental Planning and Conservation, or a BA major concentration in Global Sustainable Systems. The department also offers a BA major designed for double major students in Elementary Education. The department offers a minor in Geography and coordinates two interdisciplinary minor programs: Geographic Information Systems and Urban Studies and Planning. Department faculty are focused on delivering programs that help students build understanding about how humans intersect with the natural world. Geography majors learn a broad range of skills and knowledge applicable in a broad range of career opportunities. Bridgewater State University ( BSU ) currently has 11,000 full-time students that are a mix of residential and commuter students, and a high proportion of whom are the first in their family to attend college. The university and the department are strongly committed to our students and their success. https://www.bridgew.edu/bsuvalues Essential Duties The Department of Geography at Bridgewater State University seeks qualified Part Time Faculty who are enthusiastic teachers and dedicated to working with undergraduates for the Spring 2027 semester. Courses may include Introduction to Physical Geography lecture and lab, Human Geography, Physical Geography and Geographic Information Systems. Applicants should possess: Enthusiasm for teaching and dedication to working with undergraduates. Sensitivity to and understanding of students from diverse backgrounds with a wide range of abilities. Skill in using technology effectively in teaching and learning. Ability to teach in-person, on campus. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Geography or closely related discipline is required. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience at the university level preferred. PhD in Geography or closely related field preferred. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00664P Open Date 10/01/2026 Close Date 02/28/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Geography Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Teaching Statement Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33965": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Department of Special Education", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Assistant Professor, Department of Special Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Assistant Professor, Department of Special Education Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. Curriculum Vita (CV) Cover letter Teaching statement- Applicants are required to submit a teaching statement that reflects their philosophy and practices related to teaching and learning in higher education. The statement should discuss instructional methods, student engagement, assessment of learning outcomes, and commitment to creating an inclusive, supportive, and effective learning environment for diverse student populations. Please provide information on previous SPED licensure, documented school experience and a current BCBA certification number in your application materials. Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor, Department of Special Education Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Department Summary The Department of Special Education at Bridgewater State University ( BSU ) invites applications for the position of full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Special Education. The mission of the department is to prepare special educators and related professionals to teach, lead, and serve in a diverse and evolving global society. The department offers programs designed to meet the needs of undergraduate students who are interested in obtaining Massachusetts initial licensure area of Teacher of Students with Moderate Disabilities (PreK-2, PreK-8, or 5-12) or as a Teacher of Students with Severe Disabilities (PreK-2, or all levels). The department also offers two minors designed to meet the needs of undergraduate students who have an interest in students with disabilities. At the graduate level the department offers nine different M.Ed. programs that provide initial and professional licenses in Moderate and Severe disabilities, non-licensure, and qualifications as a Board Certified Behavior Analyst. There are also four certificate programs for transition specialists, autism, social emotional learning, and applied behavior analysis. The Department supports a variety of off-campus cohort programs that provide qualifications for licensure, complete M.Ed. programs, or complete certificate programs. The Department is growing its leadership capacity for this Applied Behavior Analysis ( ABA ) programming and is seeking a faculty member to guide the M.Ed. pathway to Board Certified Behavior Analyst ( BCBA ) certification and the graduate ABA certificate program. The special education licensure programs at Bridgewater State University meet all Massachusetts Department of Education licensure requirements and standards established by the Council of Exceptional Children ( CEC ). The department\u2019s Applied Behavior Analysis coursework is designed to align with standards set by the Behavior Analyst Certification Board ( BACB ). The Department of Special Education at Bridgewater State University is part of a cohesive campus community that provides professional opportunities for faculty advancement in teaching and scholarship and a clear path to tenure. Funding for faculty scholarship is available through the Center for the Advancement of Research and Scholarship as well as the Office of Teaching and Learning. There is also a significant institutional commitment to undergraduate research and international engagement. Bridgewater State University is committed to supporting diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging among its faculty, staff and students, and to strengthening a justice-informed identity as identified in our strategic plan. This emphasis is reflected throughout the University\u2019s curricular and co-curricular activities. The University values scholarship and other ways in which faculty express their professional contributions and accomplishments. This flexibility sustains the need for faculty excellence, while also recognizing the diversity of talents and interests of our faculty as they move up the tenure ladder. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the Commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment to equity, and inclusion is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of Special Education invites applications for a tenure track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin in September of 2027. The successful candidate will work with undergraduate and graduate students. Teaching responsibility include undergraduate Special Education major and graduate programs, both in licensure and non-licensure, supervising student practicum, and advising undergraduate and graduate students. The successful candidate will model effective practices relating to diversity, equity, and inclusion. Other responsibilities include academic advising and practicum supervision in the department\u2019s teacher licensure programs. The successful applicant will collaborate with departmental faculty and engage with College of Education & Health Sciences colleagues and other internal and external partners on the assessment, refinement, and expansion of existing programs. This position requires regularly scheduled office hours for student consultation. In addition to the responsibilities above, the successful candidate will serve as lead faculty and program coordinator for the department\u2019s BCBA -qualifying coursework and Applied Behavior Analysis certificate program. This includes ensuring the curriculum meets Behavior Analyst Certification Board ( BACB ) Verified Course Sequence ( VCS ) requirements and current task list standards; coordinating supervised fieldwork and practicum placements for students pursuing BCBA certification; and leading efforts to secure, maintain, or renew BACB program approval, including any transition to BACB Pathway 1 accreditation requirements. Required Qualifications Earned PhD or Ed.D. in Education or closely related discipline from an accredited university by September 1, 2027, along with documented coursework highly relevant to special education teacher education. Successful applicants must provide official transcripts documenting academic credentials required for the position as a condition of employment. Minimum three years experience teaching students with disabilities in P-12 settings. Commitment to public higher education. Experience in assessing and teaching courses in teacher education at the college/university level to ensure the best possible learning outcomes for teacher candidates. Ability to advise students working towards the Massachusetts special education licensure endorsement for teachers of students with moderate and severe disabilities. Demonstrated ability to design and teach online, and incorporate technology use into student learning. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching and advising; to working in a university community that embraces diversity, equity, inclusion, belonging and multiple perspectives; and to excellence in PreK-12 education for all. Effective interpersonal, collaboration, and oral and written communication skills with students and colleagues, including those from diverse racial, ethnic, and linguistic backgrounds. Current, active certification as a Board Certified Behavior Analyst ( BCBA ) or BCBA -D, in good standing with the Behavior Analyst Certification Board. Experience providing BACB -compliant supervision to Registered Behavior Technicians (RBTs) or individuals pursuing BCBA certification. Preferred Qualifications Preference given to individuals with: Content knowledge and teaching experience in literacy across the lifespan. Demonstrated expertise in special education assessment (psychometrician). Expertise in cultural and linguistically sustaining pedagogy. Experience and/or knowledge of the special education teacher licensure processes in Massachusetts. Evidence of scholarly activity and contribution to the content of the discipline. Experience designing, coordinating, or securing BACB approval for a Verified Course Sequence ( VCS ) or comparable ABA / BCBA program. Experience leading or growing an Applied Behavior Analysis or BCBA -preparation program at the college/university level. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. At present, the university can only sponsor employment-based visas, including H1-B petitions, that are not subject to the current $100,000 fee or any other similar or related fees imposed through U.S. immigration regulations, laws, executive orders, etc. The university will continue to monitor the ongoing changes in U.S. immigration regulations and it reserves the right to modify this policy as the regulatory and legal landscapes change. Salary is commensurate with experience in accordance with the Appendix O of the MSCA contract . A reasonable starting salary range to expect for a new faculty member appointed at the rank of Assistant Professor is $75,000 to $85,000. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00651P Open Date 08/18/2026 Close Date 11/08/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. Curriculum Vita (CV) Cover letter Teaching statement- Applicants are required to submit a teaching statement that reflects their philosophy and practices related to teaching and learning in higher education. The statement should discuss instructional methods, student engagement, assessment of learning outcomes, and commitment to creating an inclusive, supportive, and effective learning environment for diverse student populations. Please provide information on previous SPED licensure, documented school experience and a current BCBA certification number in your application materials. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33963": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Management/Human Resource Management, Department of Management and Marketing", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Assistant Professor of Management/Human Resource Management, Department of Management and Marketing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Assistant Professor of Management/Human Resource Management, Department of Management and Marketing Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Statement of teaching experience, interests, and philosophy. Research statement describing the candidate's current research agenda and plans for continued scholarly activity. Evidence of teaching effectiveness (for example, summaries of student evaluations, peer observations, or other relevant documentation). Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor of Management/Human Resource Management, Department of Management and Marketing Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Department Summary The Management & Marketing Department is seeks applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Management/Human Resources beginning Fall 2027. The Department of Management and Marketing at Bridgewater State University educates students for successful careers in business and management through high-quality education. The Department offers a Bachelor of Science in Management with concentrations in General Management, Global Management, Human Resources Management, Information Systems Management, and Operations Management, as well as a Bachelor of Science in Marketing. The Department also contributes to the University\u2019s Master of Business Administration ( MBA ) program. The Department is committed to high-quality teaching and student success. Students benefit from small class sizes, internships, experiential and project-based learning, employer connections, and opportunities to apply classroom learning to real organizational challenges. The successful candidate will join a collegial faculty committed to excellence in teaching, scholarship, advising, and service and will contribute broadly to the undergraduate Management curriculum, particularly in General Management and Human Resource Management, while also contributing as needed to the MBA program. Bridgewater State University is a welcoming, compassionate and intellectually rigorous learning, working and living environment, committed to the success of every student. We value our commitment to equalizing educational opportunity for all-for each and every student. Students in the Management and Marketing department consists of 49% first generation students, 39% students of color, 9% openly LGBTQ+ students, 34% low-income students and 3% Veteran students. Bridgewater State University aspires to be a community where all students, regardless of socioeconomic background, have full and equal access to the educational opportunities and social experiences that best prepare and inspire them to build purposeful lives of their choosing. Our department is supportive and engaging, offering the successful candidate, who reflects our values and commitment to the success of every student at BSU , a place for to thrive. Essential Duties The Department of Management and Marketing at Bridgewater State University seeks applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Management beginning Fall 2027. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, scholarship, academic advising, and service. The primary teaching responsibility will be at the undergraduate level. The successful candidate must be prepared to teach courses across both the General Management and Human Resource Management curricula. General Management teaching assignments may include Principles of Management, Organizational Behavior, Leadership, and Strategic Management. Human Resource Management teaching assignments may include Staffing, Compensation Management, Training and Development, and Labor Relations. The successful candidate may also have opportunities to teach courses in the University\u2019s MBA program. The successful candidate will be expected to maintain an active program of scholarly activity consistent with the University\u2019s expectations for tenure and promotion. The candidate will also participate in academic advising and contribute to the ongoing development and assessment of departmental programs and curricula. Essential duties also include participation in departmental and University meetings, committee work, curriculum development, student advising and mentoring, and other forms of service to the Department, College, University, profession, and broader community. The ideal candidate must demonstrate sensitivity to and an understanding of students from diverse backgrounds with a wide range of abilities. Required Qualifications An earned Ph.D. or DBA in Management, Human Resource Management, Organizational Behavior, Business Administration or a closely related business discipline, or a Ph.D. in Industrial/Organizational Psychology, from an accredited institution by September 1, 2027. College-level teaching experience with undergraduate students. Academic preparation and expertise sufficient to teach courses in both General Management and Human Resource Management. Evidence of, or demonstrated potential for, an active and sustainable program of scholarly research. A strong commitment to excellence in teaching, academic advising, and student success. Ability to work collaboratively with colleagues and contribute to departmental and University service. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 College-level teaching experience in multiple areas of General Management and/or Human Resource Management. \u2022 Experience teaching graduate-level business, management, human resource management, organizational behavior, leadership, or related courses. \u2022 Evidence of scholarly productivity, preferably including publications in peer-reviewed/refereed academic journals. \u2022 A clearly defined research agenda with the potential for continued scholarly productivity. \u2022 Professional or organizational experience related to management or human resource management. \u2022 Experience with experiential, applied, or project-based learning. \u2022 Excellent written and oral communication skills. \u2022 Knowledge of, or openness to further developing culturally responsive pedagogical techniques and effective practices to engage a diverse group of students. \u2022 Familiarity with, or openness to adopting, innovative instructional technologies to foster engaged learning. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. At present, the university can only sponsor employment-based visas, including H1-B petitions, that are not subject to the current $100,000 fee or any other similar or related fees imposed through U.S. immigration regulations, laws, executive orders, etc. The university will continue to monitor the ongoing changes in U.S. immigration regulations and it reserves the right to modify this policy as the regulatory and legal landscapes change. Salary is commensurate with experience in accordance with the Appendix O of the MSCA contract . A reasonable starting salary range to expect for a new faculty member appointed at the rank of Assistant Professor is $75,000 to $85,000. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00660P Open Date 09/25/2026 Close Date 11/25/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Statement of teaching experience, interests, and philosophy. Research statement describing the candidate\u2019s current research agenda and plans for continued scholarly activity. Evidence of teaching effectiveness (for example, summaries of student evaluations, peer observations, or other relevant documentation). Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Research Statement Related Professional Materials Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33962": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Photonics -Department of Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Assistant Professor, Photonics -Department of Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Assistant Professor, Photonics -Department of Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement Research Statement Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor, Photonics -Department of Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Department Summary The Department of Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering at Bridgewater State University ( BSU ) is an active and growing department. We have approximately 90 majors. The Photonics program is a new major concentration and was recently granted full accreditation by ABET for six years. The successful candidate will join a department that values teaching and conducting research with undergraduate students. The department has a broad and expanding breadth of theoretical and experimental based courses with research lab spaces housed in the $98M Dana Mohler-Faria Science Building. The Physics program at BSU has been recognized nationally for its strong number of majors and graduates (average 12 per year) and is now graduating an additional 5 or more students per year in Photonics and Optical Engineering. These numbers reflect a strong student-workforce development history with ties to Photonics/Optics related industries, top graduate schools (most recently in biophysics, particle physics, quantum technologies, astronomy and general relativity) while continuing our tradition of training high school teachers. Undergraduates in the department come from a mix of backgrounds and identities, with 46% first generation students, 32% students of color, 25% female students, and 14% openly LGBTQIA+ students. The Photonics program has created new paths and opportunities for our graduates in both physics and photonics. The Department has strong connections and collaborations with local laboratories and companies along with a working relationship with AIM Photonics and the region\u2019s AIM Photonics LEAP (Labs for Education and Application Prototypes) Academies. Students can join two student groups, BEAM (Bridgewater Emission and Absorption Manipulators) a Chapter in Optica and the Society of Physics Students (American Institute of Physics). The Department of Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering embraces diversity and inclusion and is an inaugural member of the APS IDEA (Inclusion, Diversity, and Equity Alliance) network. The successful candidate will work with their colleagues in advancing the mission of the department in serving and supporting our racially and ethnically diverse campus community. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering invites applications for a full-time, tenure track position of Assistant Professor in the field of Photonics or Optical Engineering. The Department seeks candidates that can complement our existing capabilities, with skills in areas such as optical engineering (system design, signal processing, image processing, and modern optics hardware), semiconductor devices, fiber optics, quantum optics, and digital devices. Strong candidates will demonstrate the ability to bring industry-sponsored projects into the Senior Design course, engage majors in meaningful undergraduate research opportunities, and contribute to the department\u2019s longstanding commitment to assessment, continuous improvement, and accreditation. The successful candidate will be a dedicated and passionate teacher. Department needs require that the new faculty member be flexible enough to teach mission critical courses in the college\u2019s core curriculum as well as courses in the physics and photonics major. The ideal candidate will teach both lectures and labs. The candidate will join their department colleagues in continuing to develop the overall vision for the photonics program. This includes assessment duties and working to foster connections with local labs and companies in effort to provide our students with internships, co-ops and senior design projects. The successful candidate will contribute to a department culture that is inclusive, student-centered and energetic, and which emphasizes experiences outside of the classroom. Required Qualifications A Ph.D. in Photonics Engineering, Physics, Optical Engineering, or Electrical Engineering specializing in optics or related fields is required by September 1, 2027. Applicants should have teaching experience and be strongly committed to excellence in teaching, advising, and research with undergraduate students. Applicants should be committed to working in a multicultural environment that fosters diversity. Applicants should have an ability to communicate effectively in speaking and writing, to use technology effectively in teaching and learning, and to work collaboratively. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of post-doctoral and/or industry work demonstrating the ability to support and mentor research appropriate at the undergraduate level. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. At present, the university can only sponsor employment-based visas, including H1-B petitions, that are not subject to the current $100,000 fee or any other similar or related fees imposed through U.S. immigration regulations, laws, executive orders, etc. The university will continue to monitor the ongoing changes in U.S. immigration regulations and it reserves the right to modify this policy as the regulatory and legal landscapes change. Salary is commensurate with experience in accordance with the Appendix O of the MSCA contract . A reasonable starting salary range to expect for a new faculty member appointed at the rank of Assistant Professor is $75,000 to $85,000. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00656P Open Date 09/25/2026 Close Date 01/04/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement Research Statement Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Research Statement Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33961": {"title": "Assistant Professor- Critical Corrections and Prison Education, Department of Criminal Justice", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Assistant Professor- Critical Corrections and Prison Education, Department of Criminal Justice Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Assistant Professor- Critical Corrections and Prison Education, Department of Criminal Justice Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. Cover letter CV Statement of teaching philosophy and experience, including information related to experience and interest in using inclusive and impactful teaching strategies and techniques for including students with varied backgrounds and learning styles Statement regarding research agenda and plan, including interest in capacity for supervising undergraduate research Equity and Inclusion Statement- a personal statement on a candidate\u2019s past efforts to enhance diversity, equity, and inclusion. The equity and inclusion statement is an opportunity for candidates to discuss scholarship, professional skills, and demonstrable experience that would enhance the university\u2019s efforts to promote a diverse, equitable, and inclusive community. Equity and inclusion statements will be considered as part of a transparent and comprehensive review of candidates\u2019 application materials. Instructional artifact, like a syllabus, lesson plan or other materials that demonstrate a capacity to engage with and support students with varied backgrounds and learning styles Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor- Critical Corrections and Prison Education, Department of Criminal Justice Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Department Summary Bridgewater State University\u2019s Department of Criminal Justice invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position to begin Fall 2027. The department seeks a collaborative teacher/scholar who is student-oriented and committed to an environment that acknowledges, encourages, and respects diversity and difference. The ideal candidate will be committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, scholarship, and service. The Department enrolls more than 600 undergraduate majors, a third of whom are students of color. It houses a Victimology concentration, a Youth and Juvenile justice concentration and a Racial and Social Justice concentration in addition to the BS in Criminal Justice and is home to a vibrant graduate program including offerings in cyber criminology and cybersecurity. The Department of Criminal Justice is a diverse, dynamic, interdisciplinary department with a strong focus on critical thought, undergraduate research, social justice and equity, where each member of the faculty is committed to providing a meaningful, educational experience to every single student, one student at a time. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties Bridgewater State University has a 4-4 teaching responsibility (most often i mplemented with a three-course preparation) supported with significant professional development opportunities and guidance. The successful candidate will be expected to teach a variety of criminal justice courses, with preference given to candidates who have experience teaching courses in one or more of the following areas: prison education or corrections. Additionally, student advising, service to the department and working with students on undergraduate research are essential duties. The successful candidate will also demonstrate a record of scholarly inquiry and a commitment to inclusive, student-centered teaching. We are particularly interested in candidates who use high-impact active learning teaching strategies that inspire and support students from diverse backgrounds and in possession of different gifts. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Criminal Justice or Criminology by September 1, 2027. Other closely related fields may be considered. A law degree alone does not meet the terminal degree requirement for this position. The successful applicant will offer evidence of involvement with prison education programs like Inside/Out, scholarly activity and teaching experience related to corrections/penology, and/or activism/service regarding reentry, decarceration or abolition. Applicants should be deeply committed to excellence in teaching, social justice, mentoring, and to working in a multicultural environment that fosters diversity, equity, and inclusion. They must also have a commitment to public higher education, to innovative and impactful teaching strategies, and to meaningful collaboration. The successful applicant will demonstrate an ability to use technology effectively in teaching and learning and can offer evidence of an active scholarly agenda. Applicants must demonstrate an ability to dialogue impactfully with students from diverse backgrounds with a wide range of abilities. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience in higher education, including with hybrid and online teaching formats, is preferred. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. At present, the university can only sponsor employment-based visas, including H1-B petitions, that are not subject to the current $100,000 fee or any other similar or related fees imposed through U.S. immigration regulations, laws, executive orders, etc. The university will continue to monitor the ongoing changes in U.S. immigration regulations and it reserves the right to modify this policy as the regulatory and legal landscapes change. Salary is commensurate with experience in accordance with the Appendix O of the MSCA contract . A reasonable starting salary range to expect for a new faculty member appointed at the rank of Assistant Professor is $75,000 to $85,000. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00659P Open Date 09/25/2026 Close Date 11/25/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. Cover letter CV Statement of teaching philosophy and experience, including information related to experience and interest in using inclusive and impactful teaching strategies and techniques for including students with varied backgrounds and learning styles Statement regarding research agenda and plan, including interest in capacity for supervising undergraduate research Equity and Inclusion Statement- a personal statement on a candidate\u2019s past efforts to enhance diversity, equity, and inclusion. The equity and inclusion statement is an opportunity for candidates to discuss scholarship, professional skills, and demonstrable experience that would enhance the university\u2019s efforts to promote a diverse, equitable, and inclusive community. Equity and inclusion statements will be considered as part of a transparent and comprehensive review of candidates\u2019 application materials. Instructional artifact, like a syllabus, lesson plan or other materials that demonstrate a capacity to engage with and support students with varied backgrounds and learning styles Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Research Statement Related Professional Materials Other Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33960": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Film and Video Arts Production, Department of Communication", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Assistant Professor, Film and Video Arts Production, Department of Communication Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Assistant Professor, Film and Video Arts Production, Department of Communication Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications for the position will be reviewed beginning October 15, 2026, and will be accepted through November 30, 2026. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: \u25cf Contact information for at least three references entries (names, addresses, phone numbers, emails) in space provided on the application form. \u25cf Cover letter \u25cf Curriculum vitae \u25cf One-page teaching statement describing the applicant\u2019s pedagogical strengths, approaches to mentoring undergraduate students, and specific strategies for fostering an equitable and inclusive learning environment \u25cf One-page statement outlining the applicant\u2019s creative or scholarly work, artistic approaches, and future creative direction \u25cf Portfolio with 2-3 publicly accessible links to video or other media that best represent the applicant\u2019s production work, identifying each work and the applicant\u2019s role in its creation For specific questions about the position and application process, please contact the search committee chair, Colleen Kelly Poplin at cpoplin@bridgew.edu. Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor, Film and Video Arts Production, Department of Communication Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Department Summary The Department of Communication at Bridgewater State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Film and Video Arts Production beginning Fall 2027. The Department of Communication offers three majors: Film and Video Arts Production, Communication and Media Studies, and Public Relations. The department currently serves over three hundred undergraduate majors, including more than one hundred students enrolled in Film and Video Arts Production. We are a thoughtful, collegial department committed to preparing students to meaningfully engage with their communities and the wider world. Our students bring a wide range of experiences and perspectives to their creative work. As of Spring 2026, half of our FVAP majors are first-generation college students, 43% are commuters, and 30% come from low-income backgrounds. Additionally, 32.5% identify as women, 26.3% identify as students of color, and 17% identify as LGBTQIA+. Film and Video Arts Production is a growing major that combines technical training with a broad academic foundation in film and media. Students develop original work while building the creative confidence, technical skills, and collaborative practices needed to bring their visions to life. Our program offers foundational video production courses and specialized study in areas such as screenwriting, sound, editing, and cinematography. This is an exciting time to join us: we are undertaking a significant renovation of our production facilities while continuing to strengthen the major. We are looking for a colleague who will expand students\u2019 technical capabilities, contribute to the ongoing development of our curriculum and facilities, and help shape the program\u2019s future. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the Commonwealth, and the world. BSU has worked to ensure that our students receive an accessible, affordable, and exceptional education. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Those committed to working in a diverse cultural environment are strongly encouraged to apply. Essential Duties Essential Duties We seek an educator and practitioner with strong technical expertise in film and video production. Candidates with expertise in digital cinematography and/or digital post-production are especially encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will teach courses across the Film and Video Arts Production curriculum, including Film/Video Production I and II, Cinematography, Advanced Video Editing, and other courses aligned with the candidate\u2019s strengths and the evolving needs of the program. The candidate will also contribute to the university\u2019s Core Curriculum by teaching film and media studies courses for students from across the university. The successful candidate will teach in-person courses in the fall and spring semesters, with a standard teaching load of four 3-credit courses per semester. The position includes advising and mentoring undergraduate students, department and university service, and participation in shared program responsibilities. These responsibilities may include supporting the Filmmakers Society, the annual student showcase and awards, and other student-focused initiatives. The candidate will also maintain an active creative practice and/or scholarly agenda appropriate to their area of expertise. Required Qualifications Required Qualifications: \u25cf MFA or PhD in Film/Video Production, Media Production, Communication, or a related discipline by September 1, 2027 \u25cf Experience in video production, cinematography, and/or digital post-production \u25cf Experience teaching undergraduate courses Preferred Qualifications Preferred Qualifications: Teaching \u25cf Ability to translate technical concepts into accessible and engaging learning experiences \u25cf Experience advancing access, equity, and student success in higher education \u25cf Experience with experiential, project-based, or other high-impact teaching practices Creative Practice \u25cf Active creative practice and/or scholarly agenda in film and video production \u25cf Professional experience in film and video production \u25cf Commitment to keeping current with emerging production technologies and industry practices Program Engagement \u25cf Experience mentoring student filmmakers and/or supporting student organizations \u25cf Experience contributing to curriculum development, facilities planning, or other initiatives that support the growth of an academic program \u25cf Experience developing partnerships with professional and/or community media organizations Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. At present, the university can only sponsor employment-based visas, including H1-B petitions, that are not subject to the current $100,000 fee or any other similar or related fees imposed through U.S. immigration regulations, laws, executive orders, etc. The university will continue to monitor the ongoing changes in U.S. immigration regulations and it reserves the right to modify this policy as the regulatory and legal landscapes change. Salary is commensurate with experience in accordance with the Appendix O of the MSCA contract . A reasonable starting salary range to expect for a new faculty member appointed at the rank of Assistant Professor is $75,000 to $85,000. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00661P Open Date 09/25/2026 Close Date 11/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Applications for the position will be reviewed beginning October 15, 2026, and will be accepted through November 30, 2026. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: \u25cf Contact information for at least three references entries (names, addresses, phone numbers, emails) in space provided on the application form. \u25cf Cover letter \u25cf Curriculum vitae \u25cf One-page teaching statement describing the applicant\u2019s pedagogical strengths, approaches to mentoring undergraduate students, and specific strategies for fostering an equitable and inclusive learning environment \u25cf One-page statement outlining the applicant\u2019s creative or scholarly work, artistic approaches, and future creative direction \u25cf Portfolio with 2-3 publicly accessible links to video or other media that best represent the applicant\u2019s production work, identifying each work and the applicant\u2019s role in its creation For specific questions about the position and application process, please contact the search committee chair, Colleen Kelly Poplin at cpoplin@bridgew.edu. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Other Portfolio Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33958": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Department of Geography", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Assistant Professor, Department of Geography Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Assistant Professor, Department of Geography Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: * A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. * Resume/CV * Cover Letter * Undergraduate Teaching and Mentoring Experience Statement- Applicants are required to submit a teaching statement that reflects their philosophy and practices related to teaching and learning in higher education. The statement should discuss instructional methods, student engagement, assessment of learning outcomes, and commitment to creating an inclusive, supportive, and effective learning environment for diverse student populations. * Teaching Artifact-Applicants are required to submit teaching artifacts that demonstrate their ability to apply geospatial techniques to physical geography topics while supporting inclusive teaching and learning practices. Materials should illustrate instruction for both introductory-level courses (including foundational major and university-wide science lab or non-lab) courses and an intermediate- or advanced-level undergraduate course. Appropriate artifacts may include a laboratory exercise, assignment, lesson plan, instructional module, or other course material. Each artifact should identify the geospatial methods or technologies employed, the intended learning objectives, and the expected student outcomes. Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor, Department of Geography Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Department Summary The Department of Geography at Bridgewater State University is accepting applications for a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor. Our department is committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching, research, applied geography and outreach. The department offers: B.S. in Geography with concentrations in Environmental Planning and Conservation, and Environmental Sustainability and Climate Resilience; B.A. in Geography with concentrations in Geography for Educators, and Sustainable Global Systems; minors in Geography, Geospatial Science, Urban Studies and Planning; and a post-graduate certificate in Geographic Information Systems. Our department consists of six full-time faculty, four part-time faculty and an administrative assistant, and has dedicated physical/human/geospatial classrooms and laboratories in the Dana Mohler-Faria Center for Science and Mathematics. Our department serves a diverse student body, with 27% of our students identifying as students of color, and we are committed to further strengthening diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging across our programs and community. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of Geography at Bridgewater State University is accepting applications for a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor faculty position, beginning in the Fall of 2027. The successful candidate will be a highly motivated individual with expertise in physical geography. Teaching responsibilities include courses in physical geography and geospatial science. The successful candidate is expected to bring new ideas for course offerings related to that candidate\u2019s area of expertise that support the department\u2019s leadership role in applying geospatial data to problems in sustainability and resilience. A commitment to teaching excellence that supports a diverse student body is essential. This faculty member will help support the geography department\u2019s growing undergraduate programs, a new graduate GIS certificate program, collaborations with other BSU programs, and high-impact practices such as fieldwork, undergraduate research, internships, and service-learning opportunities. Essential faculty duties also include participation in departmental meetings, committee work, departmental curriculum development, and advising students in course selection and major progress. Applicants should be strongly committed to excellence in teaching and service, as well as demonstrate sensitivity to and understanding of students from diverse backgrounds with a wide range of abilities. Required Qualifications A PhD in Geography or a related field. ABD candidates will be considered provided that they will have their PhD in hand by September 1, 2027. Experience teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. Demonstrate the ability to teach lecture and laboratory sections. Demonstrate a well-developed research plan incorporating undergraduate students into a research program. Applicants must also demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, advising, and undergraduate research mentoring that enhances an environment of equity, diversity and inclusion. Preferred Qualifications Teaching and technology expertise. Expertise in physical geography, geospatial science and undergraduate high impact practices. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. At present, the university can only sponsor employment-based visas, including H1-B petitions, that are not subject to the current $100,000 fee or any other similar or related fees imposed through U.S. immigration regulations, laws, executive orders, etc. The university will continue to monitor the ongoing changes in U.S. immigration regulations and it reserves the right to modify this policy as the regulatory and legal landscapes change. Salary is commensurate with experience in accordance with the Appendix O of the MSCA contract . A reasonable starting salary range to expect for a new faculty member appointed at the rank of Assistant Professor is $75,000 to $85,000. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00655P Open Date 09/28/2026 Close Date 12/31/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: * A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. * Resume/CV * Cover Letter * Undergraduate Teaching and Mentoring Experience Statement- Applicants are required to submit a teaching statement that reflects their philosophy and practices related to teaching and learning in higher education. The statement should discuss instructional methods, student engagement, assessment of learning outcomes, and commitment to creating an inclusive, supportive, and effective learning environment for diverse student populations. * Teaching Artifact-Applicants are required to submit teaching artifacts that demonstrate their ability to apply geospatial techniques to physical geography topics while supporting inclusive teaching and learning practices. Materials should illustrate instruction for both introductory-level courses (including foundational major and university-wide science lab or non-lab) courses and an intermediate- or advanced-level undergraduate course. Appropriate artifacts may include a laboratory exercise, assignment, lesson plan, instructional module, or other course material. Each artifact should identify the geospatial methods or technologies employed, the intended learning objectives, and the expected student outcomes. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Other Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33887": {"title": "Part-Time Faculty, Department of Chemical Sciences", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Part-Time Faculty, Department of Chemical Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Part-Time Faculty, Department of Chemical Sciences Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Chemical Sciences Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Posting Details Position Information Title Part-Time Faculty, Department of Chemical Sciences Rank Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Department Summary The mission of the Department of Chemical Sciences is to create and maintain an environment for both students and faculty to advance their understanding of chemistry guided by the highest standards in teaching and learning, scientific inquiry, and community service. Of highest priority is the success and growth of students for successful careers in industry, government, or education, and as knowledgeable and responsible citizens of the world. To achieve our mission, the department\u2019s goals are to: (1) foster a community of active learners, (2) acknowledge the different goals and backgrounds of students, and (3) emphasize chemistry as fundamental to our global society. The department strives to achieve its goals by providing quality education and high-impact practices to our students. These include engaged student learning, hands-on experience on the use of modern instruments, engagement in collaborative research with faculty, opportunities for directed study and internships, community outreach, and support for professional development of faculty and students. Successful candidates will be faculty members that can work with their colleagues to help meet the mission of the department of Chemical Sciences in serving and supporting our racially and ethnically diverse campus community. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of Chemical Sciences at Bridgewater State University seeks qualified Part-Time Faculty for the Spring 2027 semester, who are enthusiastic teachers and dedicated to working with undergraduates. The successful candidate may be expected to teach laboratory sections in our Principles of Chemistry I/II ( CHEM 141L/142L), Survey of Chemistry I/II ( CHEM 131L/132L), and/or Organic Chemistry I/II ( CHEM 243L/244L) course sequences. The candidate may also have an opportunity to teach lectures in CHEM 131/132 or Chemistry in Everyday Life ( CHEM 102). Candidates must demonstrate sensitivity to and understanding of students from diverse backgrounds with a wide range of abilities. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree or higher in Chemical Sciences or related field required. Excellent communication skills and a strong commitment to teaching in an undergraduate setting are required. Candidates must also demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching and advising. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience and Ph.D. preferred. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00657P Open Date 09/14/2026 Close Date 02/28/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Chemical Sciences Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33495": {"title": "Part-Time Faculty, Department of Criminal Justice", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Part-Time Faculty, Department of Criminal Justice Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Part-Time Faculty, Department of Criminal Justice Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: * A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. * Resume/CV * Cover Letter * Teaching Statement This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Criminal Justice Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Posting Details Position Information Title Part-Time Faculty, Department of Criminal Justice Rank Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Department Summary The mission of the Department of Criminal Justice is to prepare students for academic and occupational success through high quality education. As a dynamic and interdisciplinary department we strive to advance the success of all students, community partnerships and social justice. Successful candidates will be staff members who can work with their colleagues to help meet the mission of the department in serving and supporting our diverse campus community. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of Criminal Justice at Bridgewater State University seeks qualified Part Time Faculty who are enthusiastic teachers and dedicated to working with undergraduates for both the Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 semesters. Part-Time Faculty are needed in the following areas: Early college-offsite courses Intro to Criminal Justice, Intro to Criminal Law, Intro to Crime Theory, and other core criminal justice courses Candidates must demonstrate ability to use technology effectively in online and in-person teaching, and learning designed to meet the educational, culturally relevant, and emotional needs of our students. Candidates must develop and maintain a classroom environment conducive to effective learning, and encourage student success to all students regardless of race. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Criminal Justice, Criminology or Sociology. Related fields may also be considered. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience is preferred. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. This position is not eligible for H-1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00649P Open Date 07/23/2026 Close Date 03/31/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: * A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. * Resume/CV * Cover Letter * Teaching Statement This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Criminal Justice Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33442": {"title": "Part-Time Faculty- Cultural Psychology, Department of Psychology", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Part-Time Faculty- Cultural Psychology, Department of Psychology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Part-Time Faculty- Cultural Psychology, Department of Psychology Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Psychology Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Posting Details Position Information Title Part-Time Faculty- Cultural Psychology, Department of Psychology Rank Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Department Summary The Department of Psychology at Bridgewater State University houses one of the largest undergraduate majors on campus. The Department of Psychology at Bridgewater State University offers a Bachelor of Science in Psychology, a Minor in Psychology, as well as a Master of Arts degree with a specialization in Clinical Psychology. A number of opportunities for increased engagement within the discipline of Psychology exist, including internships and practica, opportunities for gaining research experience via the department\u2019s laboratory for faculty and student scholarship, the Honors Program in Psychology, Psi Chi, and the Psychology Club. The department has ample lab space including an eye tracker and two Biopacs but does not have animal facilities for animal research. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of Psychology at Bridgewater State University seeks qualified and committed Part Time Faculty beginning September 2026, who are enthusiastic teachers and dedicated to working with undergraduates. Course offering: PSYC 230 In this course, students will learn to critically analyze ethnocentric perspectives, understand the sociocultural influences on individuals\u2019 worldviews, and recognize the factors that establish and maintain cultural norms. Emphasis will be placed on recognizing, understanding and respecting the complexity of sociocultural and international diversity including the role of power and privilege in shaping human conditions. This course may be in-person or hybrid. Applicants should possess: - Ability to effectively teach in a close, collegial environment dedicated to the teaching-learning relationship. - Strong commitment to excellence in teaching and to working in a multicultural environment that fosters diversity. - Ability to use technology effectively in teaching and learning. - Provide quality teaching including related preparation and grading. - Provide class syllabi to students enrolled in classes and to the department office as requested. - Perform other related duties as assigned and/or required. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Psychology. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in Psychology is preferred. Teaching experience preferred. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00648P Open Date 07/16/2026 Close Date 02/14/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Psychology Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33162": {"title": "Part-Time Faculty, Department of Philosophy", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Part-Time Faculty, Department of Philosophy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Part-Time Faculty, Department of Philosophy Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Philosophy Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Posting Details Position Information Title Part-Time Faculty, Department of Philosophy Rank Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Department Summary The mission of the Philosophy Department at Bridgewater State University is to acquaint students with many of the ideas that have shaped the world, better enable them to reach their full potential as human beings, and offer rigorous yet flexible career preparation through the development of such skills as logical reasoning, the ability to read carefully and analyze arguments, creative and rigorous problem solving, confidence in written and spoken argument and discussion. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of Philosophy at Bridgewater State University seeks qualified Part Time Faculty who are enthusiastic teachers and dedicated to working with undergraduates for the 2026/2027 academic year. Candidates must demonstrate sensitivity to and understanding of students from diverse backgrounds with a wide range of abilities. Candidates must be able to teach in-person, on campus. Specific course offerings: CRIT 111: Foundations of Logical Reasoning, a requirement in the BSU core curriculum. This course introduces students to inductive and deductive reasoning, argument mapping, and informal fallacies and cognitive biases. Successful candidates will be staff members who can work with their colleagues to help meet the mission of the department in serving and supporting our racially and ethnically diverse campus community. Required Qualifications A Master\u2019s degree in Philosophy or a related field is required. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching introductory logic. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00643P Open Date 06/26/2026 Close Date 02/14/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Philosophy Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/posting