acker and two Biopacs but does not have animal facilities for animal research. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of Psychology at Bridgewater State University seeks qualified and committed Part Time Faculty beginning September 2026, who are enthusiastic teachers and dedicated to working with undergraduates. Course offerings may include: PSYC 100 PSYC 336 PSYC 304 Applicants should possess: - Ability to effectively teach in a close, collegial environment dedicated to the teaching-learning relationship. - Strong commitment to excellence in teaching and to working in a multicultural environment that fosters diversity. - Ability to use technology effectively in teaching and learning. - Provide quality teaching including related preparation and grading. - Provide class syllabi to students enrolled in classes and to the department office as requested. - Perform other related duties as assigned and/or required. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Psychology. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in Psychology is preferred. Teaching experience preferred. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00645P Open Date 06/26/2026 Close Date 02/14/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Psychology Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33157": {"title": "Part-time Faculty, Dept. of History", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Part-time Faculty, Dept. of History Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Part-time Faculty, Dept. of History Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the History Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Posting Details Position Information Title Part-time Faculty, Dept. of History Rank Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Department Summary The Department of History at Bridgewater State University trains students to engage in a sustained investigation of the record of humanity\u2019s existence. Its faculty represent a wide range of specializations in United States and European history, as well as the history of societies in Africa, East Asia, Canada, Latin America, and the Middle East. History students acquire skills in collecting, synthesizing, and evaluating information from diverse sources, as well as presenting it in support of a coherent interpretation of the past. The unique combination of content knowledge and skills represented in the discipline of history allows students to develop a sophisticated understanding of human nature and human potential. Successful candidates will be staff members who can work with their colleagues to help meet the mission of the department in serving and supporting our racially and ethnically diverse campus community. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment s reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of History seeks highly qualified and committed part time faculty members to teach lower division courses for the Fall 2026 semester. Course offerings may include US history, European history and/or world history. Courses may include: HIST 132 (modern world) HIST 221 (early US) Hist 222 (modern US) Applicants should possess: \u2013 Ability to effectively teach in a close, collegial environment dedicated to the teaching-learning relationship. \u2013 Strong commit to excellence in teaching and to working in a multicultural environment that fosters diversity. \u2013 Ability to use technology effectively in teaching and learning. \u2013 Provide quality teaching including related preparation and grading. \u2013 Provide class syllabi to students enrolled in classes and to the department office as requested. \u2013 Perform other related duties as assigned and/or required. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in a related field required. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. preferred. Teaching experience preferred. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00644P Open Date 06/26/2026 Close Date 02/14/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the History Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/33155": {"title": "Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Mathematics", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Mathematics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Mathematics Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Mathematics Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Posting Details Position Information Title Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Mathematics Rank Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Department Summary The Mathematics Department faculty endeavor to introduce students to mathematics as in important area of human thought, to help students appreciate the beauty and scope of mathematics, to give students the mathematical knowledge necessary to teach mathematics at the secondary or elementary level, to prepare students for careers in actuarial science, business, government, and industry, to serve the needs of students in fields, which rely on mathematics, and to prepare students for graduate studies in Mathematics and Statistics. The Department offers a Bachelor of Science degree with optional concentrations in Pure Mathematics and Statistics, as well as minors in Mathematics, Statistics and Actuarial Science. We also offer graduate programs leading to a Masters of Arts in Teaching Mathematics. The Mathematics Department is located in the new $100M Dana Mohler-Faria Center for Science and Mathematics, and in addition to serving over 350 majors, we provide a large number of courses for the general student population. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment to is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of Mathematics at Bridgewater State University seeks qualified Part Time Faculty who are enthusiastic teachers and dedicated to working with undergraduates for the 2026/2027 academic year. Courses Part-Time Faculty may be asked to teach include: developmental math, math for elementary education, pre calculus and calculus. Candidates must demonstrate ability to use technology effectively and learning designed to meet the educational, culturally relevant, and emotional needs of our students. Candidates must develop and maintain a classroom environment conducive to effective learning, and encourage student success to all students regardless of race. Required Qualifications Masters degree in Mathematics or related field. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience preferred. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00642P Open Date 06/26/2026 Close Date 02/14/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Mathematics Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/32967": {"title": "Part-Time Faculty, School of Social Work", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Part-Time Faculty, School of Social Work Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Part-Time Faculty, School of Social Work Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the School of Social Work. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Posting Details Position Information Title Part-Time Faculty, School of Social Work Rank Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Department Summary The School of Social Work has both a thriving BSW and MSW program. Current total enrollment is approximately 550. Our programs are staffed by 16 full time faculty, more than 15 part time faculty, three field education specialists and two administrators. Our programs are accredited by the Council on Social Work Education. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The School of Social Work at Bridgewater State University seeks qualified Part Time Faculty who are enthusiastic teachers, dedicated to working with undergraduates and graduates for the fall 2026 and/or spring semester. Candidates must: demonstrate sensitivity to and understanding of students from diverse backgrounds with a wide range of abilities. Utilize an equity- minded framework to prepare lesson plans that incorporate varied instructional techniques, multi-media, integration strategies designed to meet the educational, culturally relevant, and emotional needs of our students. Develop and maintain a classroom environment conducive to effective learning. Encourage student success to all students regardless of race. Specific course offerings include: Teaching up to 11 credits per semester in both/either the BSW and MSW programs as assigned by the School of Social Work chairperson. Required Qualifications Required qualifications are: 1. A master\u2019s degree in social work or a related field 2. At least 2 yrs post MSW experience 3. Ability to use technology effectively in online and in-person teaching, and learning designed to meet the educational, culturally relevant, and emotional needs of our students. Preferred Qualifications 1. MSW degree and LICSW 2. Teaching experience in a BSW or MSW program Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00602P Open Date 03/26/2026 Close Date 02/28/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the School of Social Work. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/32966": {"title": "Part-Time Faculty, School of Social Work- Saturday MSW Program", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Part-Time Faculty, School of Social Work- Saturday MSW Program Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Part-Time Faculty, School of Social Work- Saturday MSW Program Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the School of Social Work. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Posting Details Position Information Title Part-Time Faculty, School of Social Work- Saturday MSW Program Rank Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Department Summary The School of Social Work has both a thriving BSW and MSW program. Current total enrollment is approximately 550. Our programs are staffed by 16 full time faculty, more than 15 part time faculty, three field education specialists and two administrators. Our programs are accredited by the Council on Social Work Education. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The School of Social Work at Bridgewater State University seeks qualified Part Time Faculty who are enthusiastic teachers and dedicated to working with graduate students. We seek part-time instructors to teach along with full time faculty and field staff in our Saturday MSW (Master of Social Work) program option. This option allows students who work to attend classes on Saturday in a three-year part-time program. Each cohort of about 20 students goes through the MSW program in three years, part-time together in each class. Internships typically take place during daytime and weekday hours. Classes are held on Saturdays between 8:30 and 4 PM, and the program is hybrid, so presence on campus is not required every Saturday. This is not an online program. Students in this program tend to be self-starters and many have prior work experience. Successful candidates will be staff members who can work with their colleagues to help meet the mission of the department in serving and supporting our racially and ethnically diverse campus community. Candidates must: demonstrate sensitivity to and understanding of students from diverse backgrounds with a wide range of abilities. Utilize an equity- minded framework to prepare lesson plans that incorporate varied instructional techniques, multi-media, integration strategies designed to meet the educational, culturally relevant, and emotional needs of our students. Develop and maintain a classroom environment conducive to effective learning. Encourage student success to all students regardless of race. Specific course offerings include: Teaching up to 11 credits per semester as assigned by the School of Social Work chairperson. Required Qualifications Required qualifications are: 1. A master\u2019s degree in social work or a related field 2. At least 2 yrs post MSW experience 3. Ability to use technology effectively in online and in-person teaching, and learning designed to meet the educational, culturally relevant, and emotional needs of our students. Preferred Qualifications 1. MSW degree and LICSW 2. Teaching experience in a BSW or MSW program Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00601P Open Date 03/26/2026 Close Date 02/28/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the School of Social Work. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/32792": {"title": "Part-Time Faculty, Department of Sociology", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Part-Time Faculty, Department of Sociology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Part-Time Faculty, Department of Sociology Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Sociology Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Posting Details Position Information Title Part-Time Faculty, Department of Sociology Rank Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Department Summary The Department of Sociology at Bridgewater State University helps students cultivate their sociological imagination, the ability to understand how individual and group behavior is shaped by historical and social forces; how individual problems, including their own, are related to broader social structures, including global ones; and how to work towards resolving issues of exclusion and inequality and to move towards social justice. By studying sociological theory and research students hone their critical thinking skills, enabling them to participate effectively in professional, personal, and public life in the increasingly connected, globalizing world. Students graduating with a degree in sociology from BSU will be able to think critically about the problems and potentials of a diverse society and use qualitative and quantitative research skills to envision solutions to social problems. The Department of Sociology provides a strong liberal arts curriculum aimed at developing well-rounded, informed citizens with strong critical thinking abilities. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of Sociology at Bridgewater State University seeks qualified Part Time Faculty for the Fall 2026 semester who are enthusiastic teachers and dedicated to working with undergraduates. Candidates must possess the ability to teach Introduction to Sociology, Social Problems, or Global Social Problems. Candidates must be able to teach in-person, on campus. Candidates must demonstrate sensitivity to and understanding of students from diverse backgrounds with a wide range of abilities. Required Qualifications MA in Sociology or a related field. If the degree is in a field other than Sociology, a minimum of 18 hours of graduate work in Sociology is also required. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience at the university level is preferred. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00613P Open Date Close Date 03/28/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Sociology Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/32790": {"title": "Part-Time Faculty, Department of Biological Sciences", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Part-Time Faculty, Department of Biological Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Part-Time Faculty, Department of Biological Sciences Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Biological Sciences Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Posting Details Position Information Title Part-Time Faculty, Department of Biological Sciences Rank Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Department Summary The Biology Program at Bridgewater State University offers a Bachelor of Science degree and provides students with a broad background in the biological sciences allowing for flexibility in career choices. The overall goal of our program is to expose students to the scientific process and to promote the ability to think critically and to communicate science effectively. Students are the central focus and an integral part of the Department, working side-by-side with faculty who are enthusiastically committed to teaching and research. A strong sense of community is fostered through small class sizes and individualized mentoring from faculty, and this community is reinforced through our departmental seminar series and interactions among students and faculty. Students are encouraged to complete original research projects, which often culminate in publication or presentation at local, national or international conferences. The Department recognizes its responsibility to contribute to the understanding and thinking of non-science majors via its involvement in the Core Curriculum. As such, the mission of the department helps to encourage and to support student placement in professional and academic positions in Massachusetts, where biotechnology and education are economic engines. Successful candidates will be faculty members who can work with their colleagues to help meet the mission of the department in serving and supporting our racially and ethnically diverse campus community. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of Biological Sciences at Bridgewater State University seeks qualified Part Time Faculty for the 2026/27 academic year, who are enthusiastic teachers and dedicated to working with undergraduates. Specific course offerings include: BIOL 100L (General Principles of Biology Lab) BIOL122 (General Biology II) This course covers evolutionary principles and the diversity of living organisms for Biology majors. BIOL251L/252L (Human Anatomy and Physiology I and II Lab) Candidates must demonstrate sensitivity to and understanding of students from diverse backgrounds with a wide range of abilities. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Biological Sciences or related field required. Excellent communication skills and a strong commitment to teaching in an undergraduate setting are required. Candidates must also demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching and advising that enhances an environment of equity, diversity and inclusion. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. preferred. Teaching experience preferred. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00637P Open Date 05/28/2026 Close Date 03/01/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Biological Sciences Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/32789": {"title": "Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Art and Art History- Foundations Studio Art Program", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Art and Art History- Foundations Studio Art Program Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Art and Art History- Foundations Studio Art Program Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Philosophy Link to images of personal and related student work This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Art Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Posting Details Position Information Title Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Art and Art History- Foundations Studio Art Program Rank Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Department Summary The mission of the Art Department at Bridgewater State University is to engage students in the exploration of their individual creative and art historical interests. Our faculty strives to create an environment in which students can investigate a full range of creative expressions in the studio and classroom and where diverse interests in art production and art history can thrive. In addition, our faculty is committed to providing a strong global understanding of art through direct experiences with artists, art works and architecture, as well as through the teaching of studio arts, art appreciation and art history. Studio enrollments are kept low to promote a sense of community and positive classroom dynamics. This contributes to strong one-on-one student-teacher relationships that lead to in-depth understanding and development of techniques, skills and individual styles, along with a knowledge and appreciation of achievements within the history of art. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Art Department at Bridgewater State University seeks qualified and committed Part Time Faculty in the Foundations Studio Art program, who are enthusiastic teachers and dedicated to working with undergraduates. Specific course offerings for which Part Time Faculty are requested include Studio Art courses in Drawing I, Two-dimensional Design, Three-Dimensional Design, and Digital Imaging. Applicants should possess: \u2013 Ability to effectively teach foundational level studio art courses according to the Department of Art and Art History\u2019s shared foundations program objectives. \u2013 Ability to effectively teach in a close, collaborative, collegial environment dedicated to the teaching-learning relationship. \u2013 Strong commit to excellence in teaching and to working in a multicultural environment that fosters diversity. \u2013 Ability to use technology effectively in teaching and learning. \u2013 Provide quality teaching including related preparation and grading. \u2013 Provide class syllabi to students enrolled in classes and to the department office as requested. \u2013 Perform other related duties as assigned and/or required. Courses will be offered in person on the main campus in Bridgewater. Required Qualifications MFA in studio art Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching experience at the university/college level preferred Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00603P Open Date 04/03/2026 Close Date 02/27/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Philosophy Link to images of personal and related student work This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Art Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Other Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/32786": {"title": "Part Time Faculty, Dept. of Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Part Time Faculty, Dept. of Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Part Time Faculty, Dept. of Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Posting Details Position Information Title Part Time Faculty, Dept. of Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering Rank Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Department Summary The Department of Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering at Bridgewater State University is a versatile and growing department making new and exciting strides in our curriculum and research. We currently have more than ninety Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering Majors, a handful of Physics Minors and fifteen Master of Arts in Physical Science students. Most of our Majors take part in intensive and well-funded summer research programs in astrophysics, optics and biological physics with our faculty of world renowned scientists through collaboration. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of Physics at Bridgewater State University seeks qualified Part Time Faculty for the 2026/2027 academic year, who are enthusiastic teachers and dedicated to working with undergraduates. Candidates must: demonstrate sensitivity to and understanding of students from diverse backgrounds with a wide range of abilities. Utilize an equity- minded framework to prepare lesson plans which incorporate varied instructional techniques, multi-media, integration strategies designed to meet the educational, culturally relevant, and emotional needs of our students. Develop and maintain a classroom environment conducive to effective learning. Encourage student success to all students regardless of race. Specific course offerings for which Part Time Faculty are requested include general algebra-based physics I and II, astronomy for non-majors, physical science for students majoring in elementary education, as well as upper-level courses for physics and engineering majors. Required Qualifications Masters Degree in Physics, Engineering or related field. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience preferred. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00600P Open Date Close Date 03/31/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter Teaching Statement This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Physics, Photonics and Optical Engineering Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/32785": {"title": "Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Communication Studies", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Communication Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Communication Studies Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Communication Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Posting Details Position Information Title Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Communication Studies Rank Adjunct Instructor Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Department Summary The Department of Communication Studies at Bridgewater State University offers students a liberal-arts approach to understanding how human beings come together to make meaning and how best to create and analyze effective aural, written, and visual communication. The University Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Department of Communication Studies seeks qualified and committed Part Time Faculty for the academic year who are enthusiastic teachers and dedicated to working with undergraduates. Specific course offerings for which Part Time Faculty are requested include public speaking and media studies. Courses may be offered on the main campus in Bridgewater (during the day or the evening), or at local high schools as part of BSU\u2019s Early College program. Required Qualifications Applicants should possess: - Master\u2019s degree in Communication or a closely related field - Ability to effectively teach in a close, collegial environment dedicated to the teaching-learning relationship. - Strong commitment to excellence in teaching and to working in a multicultural environment that fosters diversity. - Ability to use technology effectively in teaching and learning. - Provide quality teaching including related preparation and grading. - Provide class syllabi to students enrolled in classes and to the department office as requested. - Perform other related duties as assigned and/or required. Courses may be offered on the main campus in Bridgewater (during the day or the evening), or at local high schools as part of BSU\u2019s Early College program. Preferred Qualifications Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00599P Open Date 03/04/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. CV Cover Letter This posting is for potential part-time, non-benefited, day program faculty positions in the Communication Department. The current salary rate for a typical 3 credit lecture course taught by a new part-time faculty member in the day program is $4,005.00, paid through bi-weekly payroll direct deposit. Rates may vary for other course types based on contact hour equivalencies. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Teaching Statement Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/34021": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Macroeconomics, Department of Economics", "description": "Bridgewater State University Portal | Assistant Professor - Macroeconomics, Department of Economics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs New Job Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Faculty Life & Development Equal Opportunity MyBSU Annual Safety and Fire Security Report Assistant Professor - Macroeconomics, Department of Economics Bookmark this Position Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: * A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. * CV * Cover Letter * Teaching Statement- Please address the candidate\u2019s ability to teach a diverse student body. Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor - Macroeconomics, Department of Economics Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Department Summary The primary aim of Bridgewater State University\u2019s Economics Department is to contribute to the institution\u2019s liberal arts mission through excellence in teaching, mentoring, advising, and undergraduate research. Bridgewater State University\u2019s Department of Economics invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position to begin Fall 2027. The new tenure-track faculty member will play an important role in strengthening our current program consisting of a major and minor in Economics. The successful candidates will be a student-oriented teacher/scholars and committed to an environment that acknowledges, encourages, and respects diversity and inclusion. The ideal candidates will be committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, scholarship, and service. The Department of Economics is housed in the College of Humanities and Social Sciences but also supports undergraduate and graduate programs in the Ricciardi College of Business. Bridgewater State University has a diverse student population, 30% of our students are students of color, 45% are first-generation students, and 14% openly identify as LGBTQ+. Despite having over 10,000 undergraduate and graduate students, BSU is committed to individual student success with an 18:1 student to faculty ratio and an average class size of just 18 students. Bridgewater State University is an inclusive community dedicated to the lifelong success of all students; focused on the continuous improvement of its people; and is responsible for leading innovation that benefits Southeastern Massachusetts, the commonwealth, and the world. Bridgewater\u2019s accessible environment of teaching and learning stimulates critical thinking and the pursuit of new knowledge and deeper understanding. The teaching and learning environment at Bridgewater also cultivates meaningful and diverse interpersonal relationships and fosters an appreciation for global engagement aimed at transforming lives and improving the human condition. Our commitment is reflected in our institutional values , which ensure that all students are supported and succeed. Essential Duties The Economics Department at Bridgewater State University seeks qualified applicants for a tenure-track faculty position to teach introductory and advanced economics courses. Commitment to and experience with various forms of teaching (both online and in person) and supporting student wellbeing is highly desirable. Bridgewater State University has a 4-4 teaching load (most often implemented with a three-course preparation) supported by significant professional development opportunities and guidance. The successful candidate will be required to advise undergraduate students as well as conduct various service and research activities. Opportunities exist for participating in interdisciplinary programs as well as developing new programs, service-learning projects, study abroad courses, and research projects with university support. Required Qualifications Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in Economics in the field of Macroeconomics . ABD applicants will be considered so long as the candidate will have the Ph.D. in hand by September 1, 2027. Applicants must demonstrate experience teaching an economics course to a college/university student body. Applicants must also demonstrate the ability and desire to teach Principles of Macroeconomics and Intermediate Macroeconomics, as well as advanced topics courses in their chosen field of specialization. Applicants must demonstrate a sensitivity to and understanding of the diverse academic, socioeconomic, cultural, disability, gender identity, sexual orientation, and ethnic backgrounds present in our community and demonstrate an interest in working with students from diverse background and a commitment to improving access to higher education for minoritized groups. Evidence of scholarship in the field with significant quantitative analyses is required. Applicants must demonstrate the ability to use technology effectively in teaching and learning, have excellent verbal and written communications skills, and demonstrate a commitment to public higher education. Preferred Qualifications While extremely strong candidates in the areas of applied macroeconomics will be considered, primary consideration will be given to those with strong quantitative backgrounds with a focus on at least one of the following: Forecasting AI and Data Analytics Monetary Policy Programming for Economics Applicants with experience including undergraduates in their research and projects are especially encouraged to apply. Special Conditions for Eligibility Please be aware that employment at Bridgewater State University is contingent upon completion of a successful background check. Bridgewater State University is an E-Verify employer. At present, the university can only sponsor employment-based visas, including H1-B petitions, that are not subject to the current $100,000 fee or any other similar or related fees imposed through U.S. immigration regulations, laws, executive orders, etc. The university will continue to monitor the ongoing changes in U.S. immigration regulations and it reserves the right to modify this policy as the regulatory and legal landscapes change. Salary is commensurate with experience in accordance with the Appendix O of the MSCA contract . A reasonable starting salary range to expect for a new faculty member appointed at the rank of Assistant Professor is $75,000 to $85,000. EEO Statement Bridgewater State University is an equal employment opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00663P Open Date 10/15/2026 Close Date 12/15/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note the following information is required to complete your application for this position: * A minimum of three (3) professional reference entries in space provided on the application form. * CV * Cover Letter * Teaching Statement- Please address the candidate\u2019s ability to teach a diverse student body. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Optional Documents Bridgewater State University Human Resources and Talent Management 131 Summer Street Bridgewater, MA 02325 Phone: 508.531.1324 Equal Opportunity Employer Bridgewater State University is an equal opportunity employer and considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}}, "rows": {"https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/34013": {"school_id": 544, "posting_url": "https://jobs.bridgew.edu/postings/34013", "job_title_in_